			"notes": {
				"rationale": "I read `floß` as the 3sg past finite of `fließen`: `dem floß der Kaffee auf die Nas` means the coffee ran onto his nose. I considered the noun `Floß` for a second because the isolated form is ambiguous, but the clause structure with dative experiencer `dem` and subject `der Kaffee` makes the verbal reading clearly better."
			},
